WEBVTT

04:10.008 --> 04:11.134
Kneel.

04:15.764 --> 04:17.890
I can make it clean, or...

04:17.891 --> 04:20.059
Might I at least know
the accusation, my prince?

04:20.060 --> 04:21.352
Where is he?

04:22.145 --> 04:24.021
- Who?
- My brother, the king.

04:24.022 --> 04:25.231
In his quarters!

04:26.399 --> 04:28.734
You are a traitor to the crown.

04:28.735 --> 04:30.444
- I sentence you to die.
- No!

04:30.445 --> 04:31.988
My prince.

04:32.989 --> 04:36.076
It appears Lord Larys
has fled the Keep as well.

04:39.537 --> 04:40.455
Mm.

04:51.216 --> 04:53.425
I need milk of the poppy.

04:53.426 --> 04:56.428
I'm afraid in our hasty flight
that I neglected to bring any.

04:56.429 --> 04:58.222
Ah, the pain!

04:58.223 --> 05:00.517
Please. Please.

05:02.227 --> 05:03.520
Take heart, my king.

05:04.687 --> 05:06.231
These are dark hours, but...

05:07.482 --> 05:09.358
brighter days lie ahead.

05:09.359 --> 05:11.653
No. No.

05:13.446 --> 05:15.031
I'm the king of nothing.

05:16.282 --> 05:20.453
With raven shit for a throne
and a cripple for a protector.

05:21.538 --> 05:23.540
Oh, I'm fucking pathetic.

05:27.460 --> 05:28.795
Oh, fuck!

05:33.258 --> 05:34.676
Draw your hood.

05:52.610 --> 05:53.987
Wait, no, wait!

05:59.993 --> 06:01.618
Who are you?

06:01.619 --> 06:03.538
Simple men in service of the Citadel.

06:05.415 --> 06:07.541
We're taking these ravens to White Harbor.

06:07.542 --> 06:09.626
You're in the queen's lands.

06:09.627 --> 06:13.797
If you mean to pass,
you first have to denounce the usurper,

06:13.798 --> 06:15.424
bend the knee.

06:15.425 --> 06:21.181
You swear fealty to Her Grace,
the one true queen, Rhaenyra Targaryen.

06:25.768 --> 06:27.895
We denounce the usurper

06:27.896 --> 06:30.940
and swear to Her Grace,
Rhaenyra Targaryen.

06:36.946 --> 06:37.780
Come on, friend.

06:38.448 --> 06:40.617
Affirm your fealty
so we might be on our way.

06:45.205 --> 06:46.914
The captain said kneel.

06:46.915 --> 06:48.249
Fuck you.

06:54.839 --> 06:56.382
Forgive my friend, he can be so stubborn.

06:57.133 --> 06:58.343
They're for Aegon.

06:59.177 --> 07:01.053
Put them to the sword.

07:01.054 --> 07:03.056
- Wait, please. Please.
- It's a very lucky day for you, my lord.

07:05.433 --> 07:09.270
The reason this man won't swear
fealty to Rhaenyra...

07:11.981 --> 07:14.025
is because he is Aegon Targaryen.

07:16.402 --> 07:17.403
What?

07:17.904 --> 07:20.239
No, no, that's--

07:20.240 --> 07:23.116
What are you playing at, friend?
Always jesting.

07:23.117 --> 07:24.993
- That true?
- No.

07:24.994 --> 07:27.704
No, of course not.
These are lies.

07:27.705 --> 07:30.082
He was lustrated in dragonfire
by Rhaenys Targaryen...

07:30.083 --> 07:31.041
- No.
- ...and her dragon

07:31.042 --> 07:32.167
at the Battle of Rook's Rest.

07:32.168 --> 07:34.002
My companion is always the gifted mummer.

07:34.003 --> 07:36.421
- I am His Grace's loyal councillor...
- Always making grand claims

07:36.422 --> 07:37.714
- for his entertainment.
- ...and the Lord of Harrenhal--

07:37.715 --> 07:39.466
Outrageous fucking lies!

07:39.467 --> 07:40.676
Someone's lying.

07:40.677 --> 07:42.303
- His crown.
- No.

08:02.115 --> 08:03.658
Pretty hair.

08:05.952 --> 08:07.287
Take their heads.

08:08.246 --> 08:10.330
We'll make a rich bounty for the queen.

08:10.331 --> 08:11.540
- Forgive me, my lord...
- No, no, no, please.

08:11.541 --> 08:12.917
...but you would lose
your own head for such a misstep.

08:15.044 --> 08:16.921
This is the challenger himself.

08:19.007 --> 08:21.175
You can name your price
for delivering him...

08:22.176 --> 08:27.557
and his most trusted confidant
to the queen as living hostages.

08:29.767 --> 08:31.351
Who are they, then?

08:31.352 --> 08:32.937
No one of consequence.

08:36.607 --> 08:37.858
What's the nearest port?

08:37.859 --> 08:39.068
Duskendale.

08:40.403 --> 08:41.528
Bar them within.

08:41.529 --> 08:42.822
We'll take them there.

08:44.282 --> 08:46.034
And hire a ship to Dragonstone.

08:48.911 --> 08:50.663
I have to believe...

08:52.290 --> 08:54.459
that Alicent's offer was genuine.

08:55.752 --> 08:59.212
It is a ruse cloaked in stale friendship.

08:59.213 --> 09:01.841
The risk she took in coming here
is beyond question.

09:02.967 --> 09:04.802
And the risk she now asks you to take?

09:07.764 --> 09:12.560
To fly to the Greens' stronghold
based on her word alone.

09:14.979 --> 09:16.814
It is a trap, Mother...

09:17.899 --> 09:21.360
to lure you and Daemon into Vhagar's jaws.

09:21.361 --> 09:25.447
No! Vhagar and Aemond are gone.
They have flown to Harrenhal.

09:25.448 --> 09:28.993
And Aegon is bedridden.

09:38.044 --> 09:40.670
I could take both Aegon and the throne

09:40.671 --> 09:42.381
in a single stroke.

09:42.382 --> 09:43.383
No.

09:44.425 --> 09:46.344
You cannot trust her.

09:48.554 --> 09:49.931
Mother.

09:52.850 --> 09:54.684
Alicent came to Dragonstone.

09:54.685 --> 09:57.771
- Alicent?
- Under a banner of peace.

09:57.772 --> 09:59.064
Surely, this is not possible.

09:59.065 --> 10:01.734
The Greens know already
that their defeat is written.

10:04.362 --> 10:08.908
Aemond flies on Vhagar
to join Cole in the Riverlands.

10:09.867 --> 10:13.787
With him gone, Alicent will open
the gates of the Red Keep

10:13.788 --> 10:16.206
and surrender Aegon to me.

10:16.207 --> 10:18.750
I will then take his head and the throne.

10:18.751 --> 10:20.836
What are her terms, Your Grace?

10:20.837 --> 10:23.296
That she, Helaena,
and Jaehaera are spared,

10:23.297 --> 10:25.924
and that this war ends
without further bloodshed.

10:25.925 --> 10:29.052
That is a low price.
Do you believe she can be trusted?

10:29.053 --> 10:31.138
Get word to Lord Corlys in the Gullet.

10:31.139 --> 10:34.182
I require ships to deliver
fighting men enough to secure the city.

10:34.183 --> 10:36.268
Your Grace, I protest
this action with all my po--

10:36.269 --> 10:37.519
And Daemon must return with haste.

10:37.520 --> 10:38.896
I'll write to him.

10:40.106 --> 10:42.567
We'll fly to King's Landing
in two days' time...

10:43.651 --> 10:45.486
and take the city.

10:56.205 --> 10:58.666
Good morrow, ser. My queen.

10:59.292 --> 11:00.334
The king requires an audience.

11:17.310 --> 11:19.479
Rather to the throne room, Your Grace.

11:33.951 --> 11:34.952
Aemond.

11:41.292 --> 11:42.710
Why are you here?

11:50.092 --> 11:51.719
Aegon has abdicated the throne.

11:54.180 --> 11:55.555
Abdicated? What do you mean?

11:55.556 --> 11:58.768
Fled King's Landing with that toad Larys.

12:00.186 --> 12:02.813
No, Aegon was bedridden.

12:03.814 --> 12:05.649
Where could he have gone? Why?

12:05.650 --> 12:07.860
Because he's even more stupid
than he is craven.

12:09.278 --> 12:11.364
We must send a search party.
He needs to be found immediately.

12:11.948 --> 12:13.908
Where were you, Mother?

12:15.535 --> 12:17.745
You've not been seen in the Keep in days.

12:26.212 --> 12:27.964
I was in the Kingswood, Aemond.

12:28.965 --> 12:31.092
I have found myself
of little use here of late.

12:35.388 --> 12:36.889
And what of Harrenhal?

12:37.932 --> 12:40.225
You and Vhagar were meant to fly
to meet Ser Criston

12:40.226 --> 12:41.769
and challenge Daemon together.

12:43.980 --> 12:47.108
Aegon has left me no choice
but to remain here and defend the city.

12:49.986 --> 12:52.571
But aid is coming.

12:52.572 --> 12:54.906
Lord Ormund and 15,000 Hightower men

12:54.907 --> 12:57.367
presently march up the Mander
with Daeron and his dragon.

12:57.368 --> 12:59.744
And the Triarchy fleet will,
at any moment,

12:59.745 --> 13:02.957
ambush the blockade with a force
thrice the Sea Snake's strength.

13:08.254 --> 13:09.880
We only need to bide our time.

14:45.851 --> 14:47.686
The Lannister host has scattered,
my prince.

14:47.687 --> 14:50.690
The vanguard was smashed
and the rearguard broken and fled.

14:54.694 --> 14:56.570
And what of the golden Lord Lannister?

14:57.613 --> 14:59.531
Fled when the cavalry broke rank.

14:59.532 --> 15:02.242
Our scouts believe they may be
regrouping near the God's Eye.

15:02.243 --> 15:03.743
Then we'll continue the fight there.

15:03.744 --> 15:05.662
We must pursue them till the last.

15:05.663 --> 15:08.998
- Have graves dug for our dead.
- Aye, my lord.

15:08.999 --> 15:11.001
Caraxes would make short work
of these bodies.

15:11.877 --> 15:14.254
And burnt flesh carries no plague.

15:14.255 --> 15:16.297
That is not our way.

15:16.298 --> 15:18.175
Rivermen must be returned to the mud.

15:21.721 --> 15:22.847
My lord!

15:29.895 --> 15:30.855
To arms!

15:31.856 --> 15:32.857
Form on me!

16:43.677 --> 16:47.890
We have come to die for the dragon queen.

16:58.025 --> 17:01.362
Very good.
We've got more lions to hunt.

17:56.125 --> 17:57.710
Good morrow, Lord Hand.

18:01.046 --> 18:02.590
Has there been word from Prince Aemond?

18:03.632 --> 18:05.759
None. As yet.

18:07.845 --> 18:09.387
He and Vhagar were
supposed to have joined us

18:09.388 --> 18:10.723
back at the Antlers.

18:12.182 --> 18:14.851
We march ever exposed.

18:14.852 --> 18:16.687
- If he does not come--
- He has to come.

18:21.609 --> 18:23.027
There is another matter.

18:24.403 --> 18:26.280
One of our men has ravaged a village girl.

18:27.281 --> 18:28.616
I witnessed the events myself.

18:30.200 --> 18:31.619
Something must be done.

18:32.828 --> 18:35.039
Hang him then, if you wish.

18:36.165 --> 18:38.375
I am not his Lord Commander.

18:41.545 --> 18:46.634
A punishment is due, yes,
but also a statement to the men.

18:47.509 --> 18:50.094
That we are not beasts, but knights,

18:50.095 --> 18:51.596
and soldiers of honor.

18:51.597 --> 18:53.182
Look around you, Ser Gwayne.

18:56.352 --> 18:59.521
Look to the sky. To the horizon.

19:01.065 --> 19:02.733
Doom and ruin surround us.

19:05.569 --> 19:07.738
We will all become beasts before our end.

19:08.614 --> 19:10.532
Only if we abandon our principles.

19:19.083 --> 19:20.709
Never knew my mother.

19:23.379 --> 19:25.756
Same as most of the gutter-rats.

19:30.469 --> 19:33.180
Was kicked about more than a mongrel dog.

19:39.436 --> 19:41.897
Wished for death more days
than I wished to live.

19:47.903 --> 19:50.698
There was this priest from Essos.

19:52.825 --> 19:56.078
He fancied me. Paid me coin.

20:00.749 --> 20:01.875
To do things.

20:06.797 --> 20:08.840
He said I had king's blood.

20:08.841 --> 20:11.260
That I was born for a purpose.

20:13.846 --> 20:15.222
I liked that story.

20:16.932 --> 20:18.183
So I owned it.

20:20.394 --> 20:22.062
Ulf the Dragonseed.

20:27.234 --> 20:29.236
And that red cunt was right.

20:33.490 --> 20:34.907
And you?

20:34.908 --> 20:36.994
Where'd you get your dragon's blood?

20:43.584 --> 20:44.835
Did you hear something?

20:48.172 --> 20:49.964
Don't like this place.

20:49.965 --> 20:52.091
All this hanging about.

20:52.092 --> 20:53.926
Vhagar was supposed to be here already.

20:53.927 --> 20:55.511
We have to wait until she comes.

20:55.512 --> 20:57.472
The queen didn't say
nothing about waiting.

20:57.473 --> 20:59.807
She said, come here, kill Aemond.

20:59.808 --> 21:01.894
I wouldn't be too keen to meet Vhagar.

21:02.603 --> 21:04.937
She and the One-Eye have slain
at least two dragons already.

21:04.938 --> 21:06.648
Fight'll be worth it, though.

21:07.900 --> 21:09.068
For the castle.

21:10.152 --> 21:11.153
What castle?

21:12.071 --> 21:15.156
The queen promised to make us knights,

21:15.157 --> 21:16.992
so we get a castle.

21:24.917 --> 21:27.293
- What?
- You have to be named a lord

21:27.294 --> 21:28.461
to get a castle.

21:28.462 --> 21:30.129
- What's a knight get, then?
- A horse.

21:30.130 --> 21:32.131
What do I need with a fucking horse?

21:32.132 --> 21:34.842
- I've got a dragon.
- You'd be Ser Ulf,

21:34.843 --> 21:36.719
and men would have to show you respect.

21:36.720 --> 21:40.682
Men would have to show me respect
'cause of the big fucking dragon.

21:42.684 --> 21:44.061
I can't live in a title.

21:44.937 --> 21:46.105
Or drink it.

21:50.776 --> 21:52.569
I imagine there'd be eager women.

21:54.696 --> 21:56.573
Get more women with a castle.

23:02.431 --> 23:04.892
Did you know Aegon had fled?

23:09.229 --> 23:10.397
He was meant to be here.

23:11.857 --> 23:13.817
It's Aemond who should have flown.

23:15.110 --> 23:16.236
You're frightened.

23:20.032 --> 23:22.451
Ser Criston and Ser Gwayne
are in great peril.

23:23.577 --> 23:25.204
I fear only for our knights.

23:27.289 --> 23:28.664
Aemond should be with them.

23:28.665 --> 23:30.375
Aemond's frightened, too.

23:32.544 --> 23:36.048
After he claimed Vhagar,
he forgot what fear was.

23:37.132 --> 23:38.550
But he remembers now.

23:39.885 --> 23:43.055
He knows that if he has to face
Rhaenyra's dragons, he'll die.

23:52.564 --> 23:53.941
Ser Soren?

23:59.071 --> 24:02.031
Lord Ormund marches here
with the Hightower host.

24:02.032 --> 24:05.285
Dispatch one of your fastest riders
and deliver this to him with haste.

24:06.161 --> 24:07.578
These are the king's instructions.

24:07.579 --> 24:08.705
The king's?

24:10.624 --> 24:13.001
- With haste, Ser Soren.
- At once, Your Grace.

24:16.588 --> 24:17.965
Alyn, sit.

24:37.567 --> 24:38.902
I saved this one.

24:41.280 --> 24:42.447
It's from Ib.

24:43.615 --> 24:45.575
Such luxury is wasted on me.

24:47.953 --> 24:49.579
I've already broken the wax.

24:52.416 --> 24:54.418
And I am not prepared...

24:57.421 --> 24:58.880
to drink alone.

25:15.814 --> 25:18.775
I forget the guttural name
they have for it.

25:20.319 --> 25:23.113
But I believe a rough interpretation
is "dragon water."

25:25.699 --> 25:27.701
An acquired taste, perhaps.

25:29.745 --> 25:31.079
The queen has sent word.

25:32.581 --> 25:34.415
We are to pull five ships
from the blockade,

25:34.416 --> 25:37.335
sail down the Blackwater,
and seize King's Landing's port.

25:37.336 --> 25:39.170
She's taking King's Landing?

25:39.171 --> 25:41.088
Rhaenyra's advantage is now absolute.

25:41.089 --> 25:44.050
She will surround the city
with her dragons

25:44.051 --> 25:46.261
and force the surrender
of Aegon and Aemond.

25:47.637 --> 25:49.765
I admit I know little of this enemy.

25:51.099 --> 25:52.683
But Aemond One-Eye seems the sort

25:52.684 --> 25:55.103
who would sooner let it all burn
than abandon the throne.

25:57.564 --> 25:59.149
Rough seas lie ahead.

26:12.662 --> 26:15.707
I cannot fully mend...

26:16.958 --> 26:21.129
the breach between us.

26:22.631 --> 26:24.841
But I do accept that it was of my making.

26:30.097 --> 26:31.431
I was fond of your mother.

26:33.600 --> 26:34.601
For...

26:35.769 --> 26:37.270
whatever we had together.

26:41.691 --> 26:43.735
I did try to provide a life for you.

26:45.404 --> 26:48.864
- For your brother.
- A life, perhaps.

26:48.865 --> 26:50.325
But never a name.

26:58.750 --> 27:00.335
I am sorry for it.

27:02.170 --> 27:03.713
Sail ho!

27:24.443 --> 27:26.695
Enemy ships sighted!

27:33.702 --> 27:36.120
- Enemy ships sighted.
- What is their strength?

27:36.121 --> 27:37.705
Three-and-fifty counted so far.

27:37.706 --> 27:38.915
They already outnumber us.

27:40.542 --> 27:43.752
Put the oars out.
Send ravens to Dragonstone.

27:43.753 --> 27:45.421
Put the oars out!

27:45.422 --> 27:49.300
Take us to the head of the blockade
and signal the fleet: form battle lines.

27:49.301 --> 27:51.178
Is it the Lannisters or the Greyjoys?

27:52.262 --> 27:53.555
It's the Triarchy.

27:56.057 --> 27:57.809
Bring my armor.

28:20.499 --> 28:21.500
Commander.

28:23.877 --> 28:26.295
The Gullet has three inlets
into the Blackwater,

28:26.296 --> 28:30.174
the largest of which opens
just to the south of Driftmark.

28:30.175 --> 28:33.636
But I hold strongly that we must press
towards the southern inlet.

28:33.637 --> 28:37.181
If our armada engages the Velaryon fleet
at close combat,

28:37.182 --> 28:39.350
it will blunt the threat
of Rhaenyra's dragons.

28:39.351 --> 28:41.727
They will be loath
to burn their own ships.

28:41.728 --> 28:43.313
A canny strategy, my lord.

28:44.356 --> 28:46.942
I can see why your king
made you Lord of the Ships.

28:50.070 --> 28:52.739
You'll rule all this kit
if you wind up in the drink.

28:54.616 --> 28:58.036
My strategy is expressly
not to "end up in the drink."

29:00.789 --> 29:03.750
We will face death on this deck
before we face it in the sea.

29:04.584 --> 29:06.877
You will be glad of our armor
when the fighting starts.

29:06.878 --> 29:08.420
I know I will.

29:08.421 --> 29:11.424
The Sea Snake scouts have
raised the alarm, Commander.

29:12.717 --> 29:14.553
If only to see his face.

29:16.012 --> 29:17.972
Signal Halfjaw to take his detachment

29:17.973 --> 29:19.640
and penetrate the northern pass.

29:19.641 --> 29:21.350
- Mm.
- The northern pass

29:21.351 --> 29:22.685
is the farthest route

29:22.686 --> 29:24.312
running north of Dragonstone.
Whatever for?

29:25.397 --> 29:26.648
To sack High Tide.

29:28.024 --> 29:29.401
Lord Corlys' castle?

29:30.902 --> 29:33.153
We will require
the full strength of your fleet

29:33.154 --> 29:35.072
- if we have any hope--
- High Tide is a monument

29:35.073 --> 29:36.575
to the Sea Snake himself.

29:39.035 --> 29:42.622
Do you think his focus will hold
when he sees his treasure room aflame?

31:05.664 --> 31:08.374
What is the weather to be today, Bold Jon?

31:08.375 --> 31:10.835
Raining piss or shit,
from the looks of the messenger.

31:13.380 --> 31:16.590
Good morrow, ser. What news?

31:16.591 --> 31:18.176
Good morrow, my Lord Hightower.

31:20.679 --> 31:22.222
I bring urgent word from King Aemond.

31:23.098 --> 31:24.349
King, is he now?

31:55.296 --> 31:58.591
Aemond says we have to make camp here
and await further word.

31:59.592 --> 32:01.428
He shall join us in three days' time.

32:07.934 --> 32:09.519
So Aegon's dead, then?

32:13.940 --> 32:15.859
One king is as good as another.

32:16.776 --> 32:19.278
Have this lad bathed and fed.

32:19.279 --> 32:21.156
- Give him a good tent.
- Yes, sire.

32:25.702 --> 32:28.163
Mayhaps the weather will hold.

32:33.877 --> 32:36.337
<i>It is my fault we're in this position.</i>

32:47.140 --> 32:50.351
I strove tirelessly to put Aegon
on the throne, but I...

32:52.645 --> 32:54.564
I failed to prepare him to rule.

32:59.277 --> 33:01.154
His frailties are his own.

33:07.118 --> 33:08.703
You should have been king.

33:12.874 --> 33:14.958
If you'd only been born first,
then perhaps

33:14.959 --> 33:16.836
we wouldn't be here, but...

33:18.797 --> 33:20.882
we must ever play the board before us.

33:31.351 --> 33:35.855
That is why you need to go to Harrenhal.

33:40.985 --> 33:42.152
To what end?

33:42.153 --> 33:43.905
It is a stronghold.

33:45.198 --> 33:47.908
One that has withstood
dragonfire once before.

33:47.909 --> 33:50.662
You are no longer safe here
in King's Landing.

33:58.795 --> 34:01.213
It is well to be fearful.

34:01.214 --> 34:02.715
I, too, am afraid.

34:06.052 --> 34:07.679
I'm not afraid.

34:15.103 --> 34:16.312
Of course not.

34:17.146 --> 34:18.523
But you are the crown now.

34:20.441 --> 34:22.986
And Rhaenyra will send
her new dragons here for you.

34:24.112 --> 34:25.321
Soon or late.

34:28.908 --> 34:30.535
I am not afraid.

34:36.291 --> 34:37.791
Fly to the Riverlands.

34:37.792 --> 34:39.502
Draw Daemon out.

34:40.503 --> 34:43.840
He has just one dragon, and killing him
would be a vicious blow to Rhaenyra.

34:46.009 --> 34:48.887
At Harrenhal, you will be unassailable.

34:53.349 --> 34:54.893
Perhaps I could even meet you there.

34:58.021 --> 34:59.564
That road is uncertain.

35:01.482 --> 35:03.108
But this one,

35:03.109 --> 35:05.193
if you stay here and wait for Rhaenyra

35:05.194 --> 35:08.406
and her dragons to come,
this one is certain.

35:13.119 --> 35:14.704
You are so courageous.

35:17.165 --> 35:19.167
But I cannot lose you as I did Aegon.

35:21.669 --> 35:23.338
If I do, I will be lost.

35:26.591 --> 35:28.927
Heed me, Aemond, please.

36:07.465 --> 36:09.842
I shall host a feast there in your honor.

36:11.052 --> 36:12.679
In Black Harren's hall

36:14.180 --> 36:16.474
whilst my uncle's head
looks down from a spike.

36:44.836 --> 36:45.712
Fuck!

36:47.880 --> 36:50.591
What if Aemond
knew we were coming for him?

36:51.634 --> 36:53.720
He could have attacked
Dragonstone in our absence.

36:54.846 --> 36:57.974
Queen assigned us a task.
We must man it steadfastly.

36:59.100 --> 37:01.436
And if that is what the enemy
is counting upon?

37:12.196 --> 37:14.156
- What is that?
- Fuck this place!

37:14.157 --> 37:16.908
- What's happened?
- I'm leaving is what's happened.

37:16.909 --> 37:18.493
We must wait for Vhagar.

37:18.494 --> 37:21.121
For how long? Forever and a day?

37:21.122 --> 37:22.540
She was meant to be here already.

37:24.667 --> 37:26.626
The queen only instructed us
to ambush Vhagar.

37:26.627 --> 37:28.378
She did not say what to do
if the dragon never came.

37:28.379 --> 37:29.963
I say we remain.

37:29.964 --> 37:31.507
Who made you fucking king?

37:32.133 --> 37:33.216
I don't like it here.

37:33.217 --> 37:34.885
Is that what you'll tell Her Grace?

37:34.886 --> 37:37.637
- That you're craven?
- I'll tell Her Grace true.

37:37.638 --> 37:40.974
That we stood watch and Vhagar never came.

37:40.975 --> 37:42.810
Your friend's right.

37:47.148 --> 37:49.024
You're missing the battle.

37:49.025 --> 37:50.860
The queen needs you at Dragonstone.

37:53.696 --> 37:54.697
Who are you?

37:55.782 --> 37:56.866
I'm a witch.

38:02.121 --> 38:03.748
Right. Look after yourselves.

38:19.847 --> 38:21.140
Your Grace!

38:21.682 --> 38:24.643
- There is war in the Gullet.
- Who?

38:24.644 --> 38:25.936
An armada of ships

38:25.937 --> 38:28.063
sailing out of the rising sun
from the east.

38:28.064 --> 38:29.607
They have sprung their trap.

38:35.196 --> 38:36.239
I shall go.

38:44.413 --> 38:45.540
Mother!

38:46.249 --> 38:47.999
Stop! You cannot!

38:48.000 --> 38:50.710
There is nothing you can say
that I have not heard.

38:50.711 --> 38:51.796
If you die...

38:52.797 --> 38:54.215
Then you will at last be king.

38:56.634 --> 38:58.136
My riding leathers.

39:06.561 --> 39:09.105
You are to lock and bar this door.

39:10.022 --> 39:12.858
The queen must be confined
until she regains her senses.

39:12.859 --> 39:14.943
I could not defy Her Grace's commands.

39:14.944 --> 39:18.322
You are a knight of the Queensguard,
Ser Lorent.

39:19.490 --> 39:22.410
You swore to protect
Her Grace from all threats.

39:23.828 --> 39:25.371
Including herself.

39:31.127 --> 39:32.295
Your life...

39:33.546 --> 39:34.630
for hers.

39:43.556 --> 39:45.056
Jace.

39:45.057 --> 39:46.516
Rescind your command.

39:46.517 --> 39:48.852
- It is treason.
- She has rejected my counsel,

39:48.853 --> 39:50.395
my every attempt to join the fight.

39:50.396 --> 39:52.814
So you make war with her instead?

39:52.815 --> 39:55.275
This is all the work of an ambush,
like Rook's Rest,

39:55.276 --> 39:57.569
a ruse to draw out the queen herself.

39:57.570 --> 40:00.448
They killed my brother, Baela.

40:01.449 --> 40:03.075
I won't let them take her as well.

40:10.750 --> 40:12.126
Come with me.

40:14.003 --> 40:15.796
We are ready.

40:17.423 --> 40:18.966
We can win this victory for her.

40:20.551 --> 40:22.970
Was this not always our purpose?

40:47.912 --> 40:50.288
Ser Lorent, open the door.

40:50.289 --> 40:52.833
Your Grace,
it was the Prince Jacaerys' command.

40:54.043 --> 40:55.418
To ensure your safety.

40:55.419 --> 40:57.545
Open the fucking door.

40:57.546 --> 40:58.422
I cannot.

40:59.632 --> 41:01.175
Ser Lorent!

41:02.885 --> 41:04.387
Jace!

41:07.306 --> 41:09.100
You open the fucking door!

41:10.685 --> 41:12.477
You release me at once!

41:12.478 --> 41:14.689
I will have your heads for this!

41:43.217 --> 41:45.719
Crossbows, ready!

41:45.720 --> 41:47.220
Release!

41:47.221 --> 41:49.640
Archers, ready!

41:50.766 --> 41:51.851
Release!

41:52.560 --> 41:54.811
Archers, ready!

41:54.812 --> 41:56.354
Release!

41:56.355 --> 41:58.857
Barrelman! Signal the fleet:

41:58.858 --> 42:00.567
Do not cluster.

42:00.568 --> 42:01.943
Keep them on the chase.

42:01.944 --> 42:03.903
- Aye-aye!
- The fight is yours.

42:03.904 --> 42:05.530
Archers, ready!

42:05.531 --> 42:07.574
Archers, go!

42:07.575 --> 42:08.658
Loose!

42:08.659 --> 42:10.328
Flagship's been sighted, m'lord.

42:11.370 --> 42:12.620
It's the <i>Bitchfist.</i>

42:12.621 --> 42:13.622
Lohar?

42:16.917 --> 42:19.252
Harden up and make towards her.

42:19.253 --> 42:21.672
- I want her to sight us.
- Aye, m'lord.

42:22.590 --> 42:23.883
Harden up! Pick up the stroke!

42:51.619 --> 42:53.161
Here she comes, lads!

42:53.162 --> 42:55.413
Our jewel in the rough.

42:55.414 --> 42:59.417
Signal the fleet.
The Sea Snake belongs to us.

42:59.418 --> 43:02.504
An equal share of the plunder
when we take the ship!

43:02.505 --> 43:04.048
- Aye, Commander!
- Commander!

43:05.216 --> 43:06.800
Commander!

43:06.801 --> 43:08.593
Ours is the flagship.

43:08.594 --> 43:10.929
We cannot give ourselves
to a singular pursuit.

43:10.930 --> 43:13.349
We must lead the assault
lest it fall into disorder.

43:14.809 --> 43:16.643
Do you think I sailed
across the Narrow Sea

43:16.644 --> 43:18.479
to win your king's war for him?

43:20.147 --> 43:22.483
Those were the terms of the contract.

43:23.734 --> 43:25.985
The Sea Snake led
the persecution and slaughter

43:25.986 --> 43:28.114
of my mates for more than 20 years.

43:29.365 --> 43:30.950
I sealed your contract for him.

43:32.660 --> 43:36.413
Tonight, we shall walk
in the ashes of High Tide!

43:36.414 --> 43:39.582
You'll all join me as I sit
the Driftwood Throne

43:39.583 --> 43:41.669
and dine on the Sea Snake's ears!

43:44.296 --> 43:45.464
Break us free!

43:47.258 --> 43:48.592
And give chase!

44:03.190 --> 44:05.275
He wishes only to protect you.

44:05.276 --> 44:07.027
I never asked to be protected.

44:18.706 --> 44:20.540
I expect it from my council,

44:20.541 --> 44:23.918
those craven men ever clutching
at their doublets.

44:23.919 --> 44:25.336
But my Queensguard?

44:25.337 --> 44:26.797
Mine own son?

45:20.142 --> 45:22.519
I may appear to have the weak
and feeble body of a woman,

45:22.520 --> 45:24.772
but I possess the heart
and spirit of a king.

45:28.567 --> 45:30.652
Enemy to starboard!

45:30.653 --> 45:32.654
- Split, split, split!
- Ballistae, reload!

45:32.655 --> 45:34.156
And put those fires out!

45:36.659 --> 45:38.326
The fleet is surrounded.

45:38.327 --> 45:40.538
And the <i>Bitchfist</i> now pursues us
with a small detachment.

45:41.372 --> 45:43.207
- Dragon!
- Dragon!

45:50.839 --> 45:52.424
<i>Dracarys!</i>

45:56.512 --> 45:57.721
<i>Dracarys!</i>

46:14.029 --> 46:16.156
Set a course through the Dragonstone Pass.

46:18.158 --> 46:20.452
The tide is nearly out.
We'll run aground.

46:21.829 --> 46:24.832
Lohar only wants me. She'll follow.

46:25.958 --> 46:28.168
Without her,
their fleet will be rudderless...

46:29.295 --> 46:31.005
and easy prey for our dragons.

46:34.300 --> 46:36.217
Starboard on our helm!

46:36.218 --> 46:38.052
Fight ready, men!

46:38.053 --> 46:39.930
Bring the grapnels!

46:46.979 --> 46:48.522
- Ready?
- Ready!

46:53.569 --> 46:54.570
Load!

47:25.643 --> 47:28.562
Call me Lohar, Dragon-Slayer!

47:29.271 --> 47:30.648
Press the pursuit!

48:33.794 --> 48:36.421
Ease the sheets and put out the oars.

48:36.422 --> 48:38.423
Cast the leadlines.

48:38.424 --> 48:40.425
Clew up the course.

48:40.426 --> 48:42.760
Leadsmen, to the channels.

48:42.761 --> 48:44.304
Cast the leadline!

48:58.152 --> 49:00.903
Depth, six fathoms!

49:00.904 --> 49:02.697
Barrelman, report!

49:02.698 --> 49:05.366
Breakers dead ahead.

49:05.367 --> 49:07.368
Tide's running hard out.

49:07.369 --> 49:09.747
Currents are strong set to larboard.

49:14.334 --> 49:18.130
Three enemy ships closing fast astern!

49:18.964 --> 49:20.257
Larboard your helm.

49:22.092 --> 49:23.593
Follow my direction closely.

49:23.594 --> 49:26.430
There is a way through the pass,
but it is narrow.

49:27.556 --> 49:30.517
Depth: half-five and fast receding!

49:32.853 --> 49:35.062
- Seven!
- Speed: seven knots!

49:35.063 --> 49:36.856
Slight to larboard.

49:36.857 --> 49:38.233
Aye, Lord Admiral.

49:39.234 --> 49:42.403
- Follow her wake.
- We must go no further.

49:42.404 --> 49:44.114
The pass is too shallow.

49:45.741 --> 49:47.743
We do not know the lay of this place.

49:49.077 --> 49:51.580
- We are sailing blind.
- The Sea Snake will guide us.

49:58.420 --> 50:01.214
- One over four!
- One over four!

50:01.215 --> 50:04.050
Perhaps 70 yards' distance.

50:04.051 --> 50:05.010
Easy now.

50:05.761 --> 50:07.054
Starboard your helm.

50:10.808 --> 50:11.724
Too strong.

50:11.725 --> 50:12.851
Ease it back.

50:20.108 --> 50:21.193
Let me.

50:23.028 --> 50:24.613
Forty yards now.

50:25.823 --> 50:26.907
Thirty-five!

50:27.991 --> 50:30.827
- And a half-three!
- And a half-three!

50:30.828 --> 50:32.662
Bank the oars.

50:32.663 --> 50:34.998
Coxswain ahoy! Bank oars!

50:41.129 --> 50:44.590
- Twenty-five yards!
- Twenty-five yards!

50:44.591 --> 50:46.884
- One over three!
- Ten yards!

50:46.885 --> 50:49.263
- Ten yards!
- We're over the Teeth!

51:11.535 --> 51:12.828
We're clear!

51:21.420 --> 51:23.754
Leave Lohar to the Teeth.

51:23.755 --> 51:26.633
Take us back to the Gullet.
We must rejoin the fight.

52:04.338 --> 52:06.589
Three hands to starboard, now!

52:06.590 --> 52:09.343
- Three hands to starboard!
- We're going to wreck!

52:16.516 --> 52:19.894
We have walked directly into his snare.

52:19.895 --> 52:22.229
Two hands to larboard now
and hold her there!

52:22.230 --> 52:24.899
- Two hands to larboard, hold!
- Cut the anchors!

52:24.900 --> 52:27.526
Drop weight and raise our draft. Quickly!

52:27.527 --> 52:29.863
Aye, Commander! Cut the anchors!

52:35.202 --> 52:36.912
What do you weigh in that armor?

52:40.707 --> 52:42.500
And the rest of them!

52:42.501 --> 52:46.004
Hold that line,
and pull the fucking oars in!

53:04.356 --> 53:07.692
Oars out and close the distance!
Bring the hooks and lines!

53:07.693 --> 53:10.444
Enemy flagship is clear.

53:10.445 --> 53:12.364
She's closing fast astern.

53:13.615 --> 53:16.075
She has the legs on us.
We can't outrun her.

53:16.076 --> 53:18.245
And we've not yet the wind
to carry us against the current.

53:19.788 --> 53:21.956
Furl the sails and put the oars out.

53:21.957 --> 53:23.416
Hard round to starboard.

53:23.417 --> 53:25.668
Ready the offensive
for a broadside assault.

53:25.669 --> 53:28.421
All shields and crossbows,
to your stations!

53:28.422 --> 53:30.048
Load the ballistae!

53:39.057 --> 53:41.935
- Boarding party!
- Boarding party.

53:45.230 --> 53:48.858
Hard about and keep pulling!
Strong against the current.

53:48.859 --> 53:50.902
- Turn!
- Or she'll be dragged back into the Teeth.

54:05.459 --> 54:06.960
She's not turning!

54:11.381 --> 54:13.175
All shields and crossbows to starboard!

54:14.926 --> 54:16.511
Broadside, ready!

54:20.098 --> 54:22.851
Positions, move! Positions!

54:31.777 --> 54:34.320
- Crossbows, ready!
- Ready!

54:34.321 --> 54:35.322
Strike!

54:39.367 --> 54:42.329
Hold that course and fucking row!

54:45.332 --> 54:47.750
Brace and be ready!

54:47.751 --> 54:49.044
Now, strike!

55:02.349 --> 55:03.683
Take the ship.

55:06.728 --> 55:09.189
On your feet! Prepare to engage!

55:30.627 --> 55:32.045
<i>Dracarys!</i>

55:40.846 --> 55:42.514
Bring down the rider!

58:20.088 --> 58:22.423
No! No!

58:22.424 --> 58:24.426
Sheepstealer, no!

58:28.596 --> 58:30.223
That's my sister.

59:48.259 --> 59:49.260
Father!

01:00:05.777 --> 01:00:06.861
Hold on, Baela!

01:00:13.743 --> 01:00:14.744
Rhaena!

01:00:23.169 --> 01:00:24.671
Sheepstealer!

01:00:38.643 --> 01:00:41.020
Sheepstealer! No!

01:00:46.443 --> 01:00:47.444
Vermax!

01:01:00.832 --> 01:01:02.125
Jace!

01:02:08.024 --> 01:02:09.859
Jace!

01:02:17.742 --> 01:02:19.160
Come on, Vermax!
